--TEST--
an `extend` block adds members and never changes how its type is built or inherited: a constructor and a `protected` method are each refused at the member, and the help names what to write instead (`rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace Shop;

extend Core\Time\Date as DateTools {
    public function constructor(int $days) {
    }

    protected function weekdayName(): string {
        return "Monday";
    }
}
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add a constructor
%A
error[E0338]: an `extend` block cannot add a `protected` method
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
